  "limitations": [
    "Scheduler Running is assignment; ISR/DPC overlap can interrupt that assignment.",
    "Outside-interrupt assignment is still not a useful-compute measurement or an exact substitute for GetThreadTimes accounting.",
    "Auxiliary CPU activity overlaps main wall and cannot be added to it.",
    "No Ready/Waiting time was observed in the DUT as Waiting; this does not establish CUDA API semantics or the cause of kernel work.",
    "Interrupts may be workload generated; treating them as unrelated background pressure or fitting the same driver overhead again would double count.",
    "One traced PID does not establish a causal explanation for all fast/slow regimes; matched controls remain necessary.",
    "Historical Nsight evidence is from a different instrumented boundary/process pair; its clocks and kernel durations are not merged into this trace."
  ],
